# Every color a Telegram Desktop theme sets, in terms of the palette. A
# theme has to set nearly all of them: 323 of the 586 keys in AyuGram 7.0.9's
# palette (lib_ui ui/colors.palette) have no fallback and would otherwise stay
# the stock light theme's.
#
# The entries were derived once, on 2026-09-22, from the hand-made Autumn
# Glass theme (configs/ayugram/autumn-glass): each literal color there was
# fitted to the nearest mix of two of that theme's roles, or white or black,
# in twentieths, and its alpha kept as the author set it. Nearly all land
# within a few units of the original, so autumn's painting carries over to
# every palette. The eight per-user colors (historyPeer1..8) are the palette's
# ANSI colors instead, since they only have to be told apart. Keys the
# hand-made theme set that AyuGram 7.0.9 no longer knows are left out.
#
# `color role alpha` is one color, `mix from to ratio alpha` is `ratio` of
# `to` mixed into `from`, and `ref key` repeats another key. A name is a role,
# an ANSI color, "white" or "black"; an alpha is two hex digits.
